{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested, evidence-only, exact R3 revision 15 head 8dfda899d98007bc02a9283e899f20b7cdfef8e4 on invitation a4b86909, original406983fe and producer bf429f06. Primary cfc695db first, corrections1334f7b7 and facts5ceeca08 all examined. Two P2 design findings remain; no P1 or observed runtime bypass is asserted.\n\nP2 — Keep authorized stop admission available when ordinary controls fill their item limit. Main6012 bounds live control items at64, with queued nonfinal;6047 makes cancel open another control;6049 requires the worker grant to apply an ordinary control;6048 voids queued ordinary controls only in an admitted cancel's outcome. Legal declared path:64 legitimate ordinary controls remain queued, then the worker key is revoked. An active admin's cancel needs a65th live control and is refused type-full. No stop operation or reserved outcome exists, and the only declared way to clear the queued items needs that missing cancel. This contradicts6168-6169 and6184-6186's promised closure. Corrections1078-1081 acknowledges the question, but adopted R1v12 at53f0e183 section6.3,1943-1952 already settles max: it counts nonfinal items and refuses an opening above it. R3's3114 outcome reservation protects only a stop already admitted. Preserve bounded room or a safe identity-bound admission/closure rule for an authorized stop, accounting for its complete item/entry duties in the existing model. Raising64 alone moves the failure. Do not revive worker authority, erase retained controls, or settle outside effects by cancellation.\n\nP2 — Bind replacement after a failed recovery to the existing person's recorded decision. Main3400-3406,6051/6118/6285 admits a worker replacement from restore-failed while restores\u003c3;6092-6097 calls it a new operation and expressly uses no authorize-attempt. The task stays running when the refused restore marks the registration restore-failed. A valid first restore can report checkpoint-corrupt; an agent with genuine current task.operate/controllerActive, no queued stop and matching hold/epoch/instance can immediately sign another restore intend without any person deciding to repair/retry. All declared guards pass. Adopted C2 at dafb5b0c section8.2,896-913 requires missing/corrupt/Git-mismatch/unsupported/expired recovery to fail closed, then a person's recorded decision, never a default: repair/new job or knowing chain abandonment. The identical rule remains at current16777d97,1590-1608; the newer head's adoption is not needed for this preserved rule. State and retain the exact binding to that recovery decision before the replacement can open. Keep first restore before readiness and ordinary host-loss recovery; no blanket new human approval gate for all restores. The finding concerns permission in the proposed rule. The pointer remains unchanged and corrupt data still cannot confirm readiness; no empty-root fallback, interrupted-command replay or executed bypass is claimed.\n\nCredit for the prior repairs: the original restore-readiness cycle is fixed by lane instance, register starting, restore-specific intend, outcome, ready (3385-3415/6050-6052). Genuine worker authority and exact hold/epoch/instance are retained; ordinary tools, pushes and saves remain behind ready. Already-admitted pause/cancel now settles by its own control-bound reserved outcome without a fresh worker grant (6047-6048/6133-6162). Stop admission at capacity is the remaining distinct gap. Stream items now hold the opening device key and continuation is guarded on it (6018/6057/6287), resolving the earlier clarification.\n\nNonblocking queue precedence: with a paused task, resume A may be queued before pause B; B's immediate outcome leaves paused, but A remains queued and6049 can apply it afterwards, making running without a later resume control. Both controls are genuine. Specify whether a later pause supersedes an earlier unapplied resume/start or deliberately leaves it pending. This is an ordering clarification, with no authority-bypass claim or extra blocking finding.\n\nArchitecture: all seven platform definitions, G1-G18, U1-U21, H1-H6, thirteen common forms and twelve substrate gaps remain owned. Signed device controls, worker operations, sessions, private activity, public work outcomes, holder/controller/agent and hold/epoch/instance/fork/task identities stay distinct. Whole ancestry and authenticated late deciding results, branch-first publication, source/removal delivery boundaries and retained unknown duties remain. Historical R3v13 with stale dependency provenance is no current source authority. R1v12 adoption and35 sends/33 results are now aligned; platform genesis acts, item-only hold semantics and scripted-capability limits are explicit. I2 delivery marks are attributed to notes/plan under review, with no source acceptance. Four named R1 asks and task/recovery reservation/evidence joins remain successor duties, with no new I2 prerequisite.\n\nSecurity: the fresh observation/grant windows and current worker checks remain; read sessions or authored text grant no control. Private custody, gateway tokens, withheld export boundaries, exact deciding identities, refusal-disclosure order, pins and unknown create/mint/delete/push/release/command outcomes transfer unchanged. No expiry, unrelated successful attempt or new ref settles an earlier unknown duty. Real device, provider, Git-host, storage and clock behavior remains owed with H1-H6 and its owners. The findings preserve those rules while completing stop and recovery choice behavior.\n\nSimplification and breadth: keep the existing control/registration/operation and retained decision mechanisms. Restore-specific admission and control-bound outcomes are useful simplifications; complete finite closure and the existing human failure choice within them. Preserve all connected browser/device/MCP/workspace/task/review/check/publication stories, person-held work, retargeting/removal, operator duties, private recovery/export and later collections/firm/delegation/cross-lane scope. Estimates are sequencing/risk information and do not reduce functionality. No extra suite, numerical quota, compatibility path, probe or Jam gate is requested.\n\nComplete evidence:863,049 bytes /8,750 LF across all3 exact current subjects. Same reader personally FULL-read prior b3 bodies, independently byte-verified them and read the complete fresh raw U3 additions/removals/contexts through EOF plus affected current contexts. Delta121,336 bytes /1,048 LF SHA256 eb998b1db642d54cc7b5cd757ae38a700b29ba2b349844703246ce74eaf19f99. Root independently read the entire delta, all fresh artifact statements/body/decisions and current critical contexts, compared all three head/path/blob/bytes/LF/SHA256/event bindings, and read the complete report. This is verified whole-subject transfer, not fresh full current-body reading. Report /tmp/artroom-checker-r3-v15-ihHQJU/report.md SHA256 b5eb821a76909cca8773389c0758a7f5c4d82afc69e505ebe6ee327d70be8e67; binding ledger SHA256 2ad7311dfd99d9d14318607fe514f0e8dad78c35d1bffc4879f3933e8706b18a. Main/corrections/facts concatenated without separators SHA256 1b8985329a4404b5e37c4167a55dd447a85a0c1347a0fd171d8893cee657d302. Full original/inherited commissions/producer basis transfers from the same personally read b3 evidence.\n\nLimits: static Git/source/docs and own metadata reasoning only. No tests, gate, build, install, typecheck, project code/scripts/imports, private diagnostics, credentials inspection, provider action, source edit, merge/deployment, adoption or implementation closure. Historical facts and producer observations remain attributed. Planner6382a82e supplied input on the recovery/capacity seams, which root corroborated against the exact documents.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cfc695db80c12aed41697bca07898ae7caded2fa","binding":"evidence-only","head":"8dfda899d98007bc02a9283e899f20b7cdfef8e4","head_news_ac